{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show HEAD:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core2.review.prompt.md | head -16'","aggregated_output":"# Code review: Axylo interaction and accessibility layer (chart core, part 2)\n\nYou are an independent reviewer from a different provider than the author of this code. Read-only: do not create, edit or delete files. Put everything in your final message. You cannot launch a browser in this sandbox: review by reading, plus Node experiments on the parts that run without a DOM (`packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts` is pure). Say for each finding whether you ran something or reasoned it out.\n\nUnder review (written since commit 5e187a4's parent; use `git show --stat 5e187a4` to see the files): `packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts`, `packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts`, `dom/toolbar.ts`, `dom/table.ts`, `dom/swatch.ts`, `dom/tooltip.ts`, `dom/figure.ts`, the interaction-related parts of `core/chart.ts` and `core/axes.ts`, the structure section of `packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts`, and the tests in `packages/axylo/test/core/focus.test.ts`, `test/browser/a11y/**` and `test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts`.\n\nRequirements: `docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md` (the pattern to implement exactly); `docs/02-product-spec.md` criteria I1–I6, A1–A10, L2, L6, L7, F8, F9, F12, C1 and the type matrix in 3.6; `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md` 1.5 and 2.4; `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` (Lookup and its comments, DatumRef, PickTarget, TooltipModel, TableModel, ReaderModel, Overlay); `AGENTS.md`. A separate review of the controller already exists at `reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core1.review.md`; do not repeat its findings, but say so if this layer makes one of them worse.\n\nFind defects, most important first:\n\n1. **Keyboard model.** Walk every key in every state on paper (default all-series mode, single-series mode, tooltip open, zoomed, streaming, paused, table open, a series hidden, the focused series hidden, no data, donut, scatter, bars): Left, Right, Up, Down, Home, End, Page Up, Page Down, Enter, Space, Escape, `+`, `-`, `0`, Shift+arrows, Tab, Shift+Tab. Where does the range input's native behaviour and the scripted behaviour disagree (value clamping, `step`, `max` when the count is 0 or 1 or changes under the user, `input` versus `change` events, key repeat)? Can focus get stuck, jump, or silently do nothing? Is Escape ever consumed when it should pass to the page (a chart inside a dialog)? Is anything reachable by pointer that is not reachable by keyboard, or the reverse?\n2. **What assistive technology gets.** For each element: role, accessible name, description, value text, states (`aria-pressed`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-disabled`, `aria-hidden`), `lang`. The range's value text in both modes and for each chart type; whether its text can be stale after data, zoom, visibility or locale changes; live regions (what changes without the reader acting; the note with `aria-live=\"off\"`); roving tabindex correctness in the toolbar (exactly one tabbable control at all times, including when controls appear, disappear or are disabled; focus is not lost when the focused control is removed); the table's caption, header scopes, row headers and pager; the donut legend; hidden-series presentation (contrast and non-color cue).\n3. **WCAG 2.2 AA specifics.** 2.1.1 and 2.1.2 (keyboard, no trap); 2.4.3 focus order; 2.4.7 and 2.4.11 focus visible and not obscured (the tooltip, the readout, the sticky toolbar); 1.4.13 content on hover or focus (dismissible, hoverable, persistent); 2.5.1, 2.5.7 and 2.5.8 (gestures, dragging, target size 24 px: measure from the CSS); 1.4.4 and 1.4.10 (zoom and reflow: wheel handling, `touch-action`, fixed heights); 2.2.2 (pause); 1.3.1 (table semantics); 4.1.2 and 4.1.3.\n4. **Pointer, touch and gestures.** Pointer capture and release; drag-select cancelled by Escape, by leaving the window, by a second pointer; wheel listeners' `passive` flags and when `preventDefault` is called; touch: tap, pin, dismiss, scroll, pinch with `zoom: 'touch'`; listeners added and removed symmetrically; anything attached to `window` or `document` that outlives the chart.\n5. **Tooltip.** Positioning at all four edges and in scrolled and transformed containers; inside elements with `overflow: hidden`; never covering the active mark; the fixed readout fallback; content when a series has \"No observation\" versus \"No data\"; more than eight rows; stack totals; staleness against the displayed revision.\n6. **Zoom arithmetic** in `core/focus.ts` (run it): scaling about a centre at the domain edges, minimum width, pan clamping, round trips, category and date axes, the wheel factor, numerical drift after many steps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
